# `Genre` subtype (`the-music-tree-genre-kit` v0.14.0 -- see `AbstractGenreCriteria`).
# `Genre` used to be a `Criteria` proxy sharing the `htmt_api_criteria` table exactly,
# hence `side` living there; it is now a genuine child table (`htmt_api_genre`) that
# owns `side`.
#
# Can't be autogenerated as a single `RemoveField`/`CreateModel` pair: Django's migration
# state renderer builds each model class eagerly as operations are applied, and a `Genre`
# MTI child declaring its own `side` field clashes with `Criteria` (its base) still
# declaring `side` too -- the two can never coexist in state, in either order. So the
# `RemoveField` is split via `SeparateDatabaseAndState`: its *state* half runs first
# (state-only, so `Genre` can be created inheriting no `side` from `Criteria` without a
# clash) while its *database* half runs last, after the data migration has copied
# `side` off the still-physically-present `htmt_api_criteria.side` column onto the new
# `htmt_api_genre` rows -- read via raw SQL since the ORM's historical `Criteria` model
# no longer exposes that column once its state half has run.
